17	/* Remote-control link: portable protocol state core.
18	 *
19	 * This layer owns the authority model of a remote agent session and has no
20	 * transport, JSON, or OS dependency. It accepts already-decoded structures
21	 * from the codec layer and decides what the device is allowed to believe.
22	 *
23	 * The remote peer is a PC-side bridge that speaks the frozen DeskMate Link
24	 * contract on behalf of an ACP agent (mimocode / kiro-cli). The bridge, not
25	 * this device, is the final authority on permission decisions: everything
26	 * accepted here is still re-validated remotely.
